<<
/Title (In today's digital world, organizations collect and share users' personal data for various purposes, such as providing services, processing information, and sharing data with third-party applications. Data protection regulations, including India's Digital Personal Data Protection \(DPDP\) Act and the GDPR, emphasize that personal data should be processed only for specified purposes and that users must be able to withdraw their consent.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 283 0 R
/Prev 440 0 R
/Next 537 0 R
>>
endobj
537 0 obj
<<
/Title (However, many systems record user consent in databases but fail to enforce consent decisions across all connected services. As a result, data may continue to be accessed or shared even after a user withdraws permission or changes their preferences.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 283 0 R
/Prev 536 0 R
/Next 441 0 R
>>
endobj
